# Every extension on the classpath is FOUND; nothing lists them in code. Contributing was a call, and
# a call can only name what the class making it is allowed to see -- the shader graph lives in `app/`,
# above the workbench, so an APPLICATION had to contribute it, and a mod's extension could never be in
# that list at all. @see com.crystalgui.workbench.extension.WorkbenchExtensions
#
# Being here is availability, never enablement: an application's manifest names the ids it wants, and
# an id nothing contributed is a logged absence rather than an error.
#
# ONE CLASS PER FEATURE. Each of these declares its own id and attaches itself; a separate
# `*Extension` wrapper beside the declaration was two files with one lifetime between them.
